The same logic holds for Bob's turn. If he gets a tails on his first flip, he wins and the probability that this will occur is $1/2$. On Bob's second flip, it will either happen for him to get a head or it won't, so the probability of this happening is $1/2$. Thus, the probability that the game ends is $p(1/2)(1/2) + (1/2) = p/2$.

Now we have that $p/2$ of the time, it is Bob who wins and $p/2$ of the time, it is Alice who wins. In other words, the probability that Alice wins is $p = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.
